From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:16:12 +0000
Subject: [M150-LTS][WebAudio] Stop paused destination and guard automatic pull
 on close

When an AudioContext is closed while its frame is frozen, the platform
audio destination is in the kPaused state (`IsPlaying()` is false), so
`StopPlatformDestination()` previously skipped calling `Stop()`. When
the frame later thawed, `Resume()` restarted the audio thread on the
closed context, and `Render()` invoked `ProcessAutomaticPullNodes()`
even when pulling the audio graph was disabled, causing an object
lifetime issue with disposed upstream nodes.

Changes:
- Call `platform_destination_->Stop()` in `StopPlatformDestination()`
  whenever `platform_destination_` is present so `kPaused` destinations
  transition to `kStopped`.
- Move `ProcessAutomaticPullNodes()` inside the active graph-pulling
  branch of `RealtimeAudioDestinationHandler::Render()`.
- Add `AudioContextTest.CloseWhileFrozenStopsDestination` to verify
  closing a frozen context stops the destination and guards automatic
  pull nodes.

Bug: 572191610
Test: blink_unittests --gtest_filter=AudioContextTest.CloseWhileFrozen*
Change-Id: I3126957a0a43ffdce2f541908ad90359e8f0fd6e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8561977
Commit-Queue: Hongchan Choi <hongchan@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Mahesh Kannan <kmaheshb@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717977}
(cherry picked from commit c26b38a137c5f813e0bc01d3781be5a16cb25638)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/realtime_audio_destination_handler.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/realtime_audio_destination_handler.cc
index c69dbce4e4430616e64e05f9f6caf9dd435a6a2f..ea98fb48dcb0a0fcea6de918f5e61d1493062f65 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/realtime_audio_destination_handler.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/realtime_audio_destination_handler.cc
@@ -274,14 +274,15 @@ void RealtimeAudioDestinationHandler::Render(
       // given `destination_bus` buffer.
       destination_bus->CopyFrom(*rendered_bus);
     }
+
+    // Processes "automatic" nodes that are not connected to anything. This can
+    // be done after copying because it does not affect the rendered result.
+    context->GetDeferredTaskHandler().ProcessAutomaticPullNodes(
+        number_of_frames);
   } else {
     destination_bus->Zero();
   }
 
-  // Processes "automatic" nodes that are not connected to anything. This can
-  // be done after copying because it does not affect the rendered result.
-  context->GetDeferredTaskHandler().ProcessAutomaticPullNodes(number_of_frames);
-
   context->HandlePostRenderTasks();
 
   // Handle audibility before handling the volume multiplier since the volume
@@ -473,7 +474,10 @@ void RealtimeAudioDestinationHandler::StopPlatformDestination() {
   // for a while. (It may take a bit of time for the destination to stop.)
   DisablePullingAudioGraph();
 
-  if (platform_destination_->IsPlaying()) {
+  // `AudioDestination::Stop()` is a no-op when already stopped, and transitions
+  // both `kRunning` and `kPaused` destinations to `kStopped` so a subsequent
+  // lifecycle `Resume()` cannot restart a stopped destination.
+  if (platform_destination_) {
     platform_destination_->Stop();
   }
 }
